      <p>
        TrueLabel implements multi-layered security controls to safeguard account records:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-slate-600">
        <li><strong>Cryptographic Password Hashing</strong>: Passwords are irreversibly hashed using standard <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">bcrypt</code> with salt rounds before database persistence. Plaintext passwords are never logged or stored.</li>
        <li><strong>Session Protection</strong>: Sessions are secured with randomly generated 64-byte secret tokens, configured with <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">httpOnly</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">sameSite: lax</code>, and encrypted database session backing.</li>
        <li><strong>CSRF Token Verification</strong>: Every state-modifying action (form submissions, profile updates, inspector audits) requires an authenticated cryptographic CSRF token to prevent cross-site request forgery attacks.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

